&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Regional Expertise: Mastery of cultural nuances across hubs like Singapore, Tokyo, China and Australia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Mindset: Strong partnership with regional sales teams to align executive marketing programs directly with account aspirations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Influence: Ability to navigate complex global structures and influence stakeholders across Sales, Product, and Communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in interacting and engaging senior leadership inside customer and partner accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience leading an Executive marketing function across multiple customer segments, including specific experience in executive content, event management, partnership marketing, and high -touch executive programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in defining and executing Executive marketing strategies that achieve funnel metrics and KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to convey complex topics simply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership and collaboration skills across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience partnering with Sales teams on joint planning, execution with key account executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record as an Asia Pacific leader, collaborating with global marketing teams to drive strategic connections through executive programs and partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding and/or experience with CRM, account-based marketing, and event and sponsorship marketing tactics and technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI user proficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced industry and work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing fintech, cloud services, and/or software solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization and project management skills and the capacity to manage multiple complex projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to craft actionable insights from complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, creative and dedicated to achieving operational and creative excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering tailored marketing content and experiences for customer segments spanning from early stage startups to the largest enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the payments, financial technology, and/or ecommerce industries and partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success delivering executive marketing programs with and through consulting and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an outsized opportunity to shape how the global economy operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Finance Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Bangalore Finance Operations (BFin) centre is a hub for high-quality financial operations execution. The BFin team partners closely with Stripe&#39;s global functional finance leaders — including the global heads of Accounts Payable, Payroll, Monetization Operations, Accounts Receivable, and FinOps Strategic Enablement — to deliver reliable, scalable, and controlled finance operations. BFin is the execution engine: we process at volume, maintain quality, surface defects, and partner with global teams to continuously improve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the AP &amp;amp; T&amp;amp;E Manager in Bangalore, you will own day-to-day operational delivery across two core FinOps workstreams: Accounts Payable and Travel &amp;amp; Expense. You will directly manage a team of AP and T&amp;amp;E specialists, ensuring consistent SLA performance, high processing quality, and strong controls compliance across both functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on people management role. You&#39;ll set daily priorities, manage team capacity, and resolve escalations — while maintaining close partnership with Stripe&#39;s global AP functional team. You own local execution quality and serve as the Bangalore execution interface for both workstreams. When you identify process defects or systemic issues, you escalate clearly and partner with global functional leads on the fix — but the day-to-day delivery belongs to you and your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Develop a High-Performing Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage a team of AP and T&amp;amp;E specialists; set clear expectations, run structured 1:1s, and build individual development plans aligned to BFin performance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire for open roles within your function; assess candidates rigorously against the operational and behavioural standards required for high-volume finance operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture of accountability, accuracy, and continuous learning within the team — model the attention to detail you expect from others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage team capacity and coverage across AP and T&amp;amp;E workstreams, anticipating volume fluctuations and planning headcount and scheduling accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own AP Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end accounts payable processing: invoice receipt, PO matching, approval routing, payment run execution, and multi-currency, multi-entity reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain payment accuracy and timeliness; manage exception handling queues and ensure aged items are resolved promptly within agreed SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor communication for payment status, dispute resolution, and statement reconciliation; maintain professional and accurate vendor relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure AP processing consistently meets quality thresholds and SLA commitments defined in partnership with the global AP functional lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own T&amp;amp;E Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end T&amp;amp;E operations: expense report review and processing, corporate card administration, out-of-policy item handling, and reimbursement cycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce Stripe&#39;s T&amp;amp;E policy consistently in day-to-day processing decisions; handle employee escalations with good judgement and clear policy grounding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll where T&amp;amp;E reimbursement intersects with payroll processing cycles; ensure your team&#39;s outputs are clean and timely to avoid downstream rework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor T&amp;amp;E processing metrics and flag recurring policy violations, system errors, or volume anomalies to the global AP functional team for investigation and remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Quality and SLA Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and report on team performance metrics: processing cycle time, error rate, SLA adherence, exception volume, and aging buckets across both AP and T&amp;amp;E&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct root cause analysis on recurring processing errors; distinguish one-off mistakes from systemic defects, and escalate patterns to the global AP functional lead for process or system remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in continuous improvement initiatives led by the FinOps Strategic Enablement team; contribute operational insight to automation and AI-assisted processing projects that affect your workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clear picture of team quality week-over-week and communicate status proactively to the Head of BFin before issues become surprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Global Functional Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary Bangalore execution point of contact for Stripe&#39;s global AP functional organisation; communicate volume, performance data, defect patterns, and capacity needs regularly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate process direction and policy updates from global functional leads into clear, documented operating procedures for your team; ensure adoption is real, not just acknowledged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate process defects and system issues promptly and with precision — you own identifying the problem and its operational impact; the global functional team owns the remediation design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Bangalore AP and T&amp;amp;E workstreams in global FinOps operating cadences and cross-functional planning discussions as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steward Controls and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all AP and T&amp;amp;E processes operate within Stripe&#39;s SOX control framework; maintain procedure documentation at the level of detail required for internal and external audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and sign off on periodic control attestations within your scope; support Internal Audit and the global AP team during audit fieldwork as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify control gaps in day-to-day operations and escalate to the global AP functional lead and Head of BFin for remediation planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12–14 years of experience in accounts payable, T&amp;amp;E, or broader finance operations in a high-volume environment; you understand the full AP lifecycle from receipt to payment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of direct people management; you know how to set expectations clearly, develop individuals, and hold a team accountable without micromanaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep end-to-end AP process knowledge: invoice lifecycle, PO matching, exception handling, payment run execution, and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with enterprise ERP platforms (SAP, Oracle, NetSuite, or Workday) and T&amp;amp;E tools (Concur, Expensify, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience operating in a SOX-controlled finance environment; solid understanding of AP controls and what &quot;audit-ready&quot; looks like in practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with AI tools in a finance operations context — using AI-assisted processing, automation tooling, or AI productivity tools as part of day-to-day operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-driven: a track record of building and owning operational dashboards; you use data to surface problems and communicate team performance, not just report status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth technology company or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to automation or AI implementation projects within Finance Operations (beyond personal usage — you helped design, test, or roll out the improvement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and proactive communicator: able to work effectively across time zones with global functional teams; you surface problems early, write clearly, and do not need to be chased for status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes This Role Exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll manage two of the most operationally dense workstreams in BFin — AP and T&amp;amp;E together touch nearly every corner of Stripe&#39;s vendor and employee spend, and your team&#39;s accuracy and consistency directly supports Stripe&#39;s financial integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll be embedded in a global FinOps organisation that is actively investing in process quality, automation, and AI-assisted operations — there is real, near-term scope to improve how work gets done in your workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll have close proximity to Stripe&#39;s global AP functional leadership and a direct line to the Head of BFin — your defect escalations get heard and acted on, and you&#39;ll see the improvements land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll build a team and establish the operating standards for AP and T&amp;amp;E execution within BFin — this is a chance to define what great looks like, not inherit it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stripe is at a scale and growth stage where operational excellence in AP and T&amp;amp;E has real consequence — audit readiness, payment accuracy, and expense compliance all depend on you getting this right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Stripe is growing quickly and along with that, so are its operational requirements. Stripe Delivery Centers (SDC) are a brand new initiative to accelerate and expand Stripe’s operational capabilities via the creation of centralized hubs or centers of operational excellence. SDC will be staffed with Stripes, not vendors - we want Stripes at SDC to have the same level of tools and systems access as Stripes in other locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is investing in building out its Creative Design team within SDC to reach users across the globe. The team designs comprehensive ad campaigns tailored for various platforms, ensuring that every visual element aligns with our marketing goals and engages our audience effectively. We create net-new creative content,&amp;nbsp; localize and adapt our content to meet the unique cultural and linguistic needs of different regions, to effectively present our message in global languages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to our work in advertising and web content, we also produce high-quality designs for presentations and other collateral aimed at large users and executive audiences. Our designs enhance the clarity and impact of our messages, making complex information accessible and engaging. Whether it&#39;s a pitch to clients or a strategy meeting with executives, we provide visually compelling designs that communicate our ideas confidently and effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Designers’ at Stripe’s SDC demonstrate a passion for captivating storytelling and great design. They use design systems to help tell compelling stories to a variety of audiences, and are well-versed at expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible design systems and experiences that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency for the brand at scale. They are user-focused, have a strong understanding of the business, and are empathetic and inspiring. The ideal candidate excels across a variety of styles, crisply articulates design decisions, iterates quickly, and collaborates seamlessly with marketers, product managers, leaders, other designers, and other partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideate, design, and produce world-class design solutions (static and motion) for a variety of events and deliverables including and not limited to presentations, posters, art, branding, and signage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can steward designers through large-scale design projects, providing art direction and ongoing guidance on creative strategy, execution, and localization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across a wide variety of mediums (physical, digital, and everything in between) to create immersive storytelling and creative content that brings Stripe’s brand and product stories to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring design concepts to life through storyboarding, comps, and creative presentations, iterating on creative based on stakeholder feedback and internal testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with copywriters, static and motion designers, marketers, and ad operations to create interesting, visionary concepts that engage a global audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor designers in design best practices and ideation, fostering an environment where everyone learns and grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present ideas in a clear and focused way that builds consensus within the team and with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive in identifying and implementing process optimization initiatives through automation and AI integration to enhance design quality and&amp;nbsp; efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 to 10 years of relevant design and art direction experience, specifically for technical and product-driven companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of independently delivering work as well as influencing the work of other designers and internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma, Canva, and the Adobe Creative Cloud suite (for both motion and statics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage a team of 3-4 Creative designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to express and communicate a brand through distinct graphics, patterns, motion, interaction, and experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on maker with the skills to effectively communicate concepts, direction, and decisions to the team and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to find a meaningful balance between optimizing for speed and quality, while consistently delivering challenging, interesting, and pixel-perfect work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persuasive and humble in explaining work, process, and decisions, with a craving for feedback to help design at your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work flexible hours, including late evenings in India, to facilitate real-time collaboration with global stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, with a drive for perfection down to the last pixel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A multidisciplinary creative with a wide skill set who is comfortable working across different mediums and crafts, and is excited about experimenting with new technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior people management experience, with a track record of hiring, managing, and developing design talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced at facilitating stakeholders to advance projects and advocate for design quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a cross-functional team at Stripe that operates at the intersection of real estate, design, and brand. We are a lean group focused on the end-to-end execution of high-touch physical environments. Our team acts as the bridge between creative vision and technical delivery, ensuring that Stripe’s physical footprint is built to an exacting standard of craft and operational excellence.&amp;nbsp; We are looking for builders who are energized by ambiguity and enjoy the process of turning a high-level concept into a tangible, functioning space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Assistant Project Manager to be the operational backbone of a physical build-out. This is a &quot;jack-of-all-trades&quot; role for someone who is equally comfortable on a construction site as they are in a spreadsheet. You will support the end-to-end execution of a project, ensuring that the &quot;drumbeat&quot; of the work stays on track and that no detail is overlooked.&amp;nbsp; At Stripe, we are obsessively user-first. We believe that every touchpoint—including our physical environments—should reflect a commitment to craft, quality, and seamless experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, we prioritize a seamless onboarding experience. Your first four weeks are designed as an introductory period for mutual evaluation—ensuring the role, team, and pace align with your career goals and our high-performance standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive momentum:&lt;/strong&gt; Attend all workstream calls and own the action items. We use AI for raw notes, but you are responsible for coordinating stakeholders (internal and external) to ensure nothing stalls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive workstreams&lt;/strong&gt;: Manage execution in partnership with the lead, from kickoff through completion—everything from sourcing vendor options and securing budget approvals to collaborating with internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be on-site&lt;/strong&gt;: Be on-site as needed to verify that our standards of craft and delivery are being met across all physical touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support team scaling&lt;/strong&gt;: Manage the logistics of expanding project capacity, including vendor sourcing, partner onboarding, leveraging AI tools, and contractor coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Draft weekly updates&lt;/strong&gt;: Turn complex updates from across the project into clear, dense weekly notes for leadership. You possess the ability to turn project noise into actionable signal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a highly organized, collaborative partner who thrives in fast-moving, ambiguous environments and makes the people around you more effective. You love creating thoughtful experiences and environments, with a commitment to high-touch, on-brand execution. You have a track record of taking broad goals, building a clear path forward, and keeping priorities, details, and communication moving with minimal friction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real estate experience: &lt;/strong&gt;You have 3–5 years of experience in real estate operations, owner’s representation, or hospitality development. You are a &quot;high-agency&quot; operator who loves the &quot;how&quot; of making things happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Users’first mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; At Stripe, we are obsessively user-first. You likely come from a background where the guest or customer experience is paramount—such as consumer-facing retail or premium hospitality. You understand that the quality of a space directly impacts the person using it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A &quot;force multiplier&quot; mentality:&lt;/strong&gt; You are a super team player who thrives in a close-knit, collaborative environment and makes everyone around you more effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High agency track record: &lt;/strong&gt;You have 3–5 years of experience in roles that require exceptional organization and the ability to navigate ambiguity. Your former colleagues describe you as the person who &quot;just gets it done.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong communication:&lt;/strong&gt; You never let an action item drop and can distill complex updates into clear, actionable briefings for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial and administrative rigor: &lt;/strong&gt;You have experience managing project budgets, navigating procurement workflows, and maintaining meticulous financial records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical leverage:&lt;/strong&gt; You are proficient at using AI and modern productivity tools to automate routine tasks and accelerate project delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Audio Visual team at Stripe is tasked with delivering best in class collaboration experiences. This role will be responsible for the research and development of new AV experiences and standards, event production and operation, and project management ranging from office builds to technology rollouts. You will be joining a highly specialized team of AV professionals working towards the implementation of an equitable, functional, and cutting edge hybrid workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and Develop our AV technology standards across our offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as highest point of escalation internally for AV issues and incidents of varying complexity and criticality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain best in class in office collaboration support through cross functional communication and partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly the upleveling and maturation of our services and process, keeping in mind scalability, efficiency, and organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly on and support when needed the production and operation of our highest tiered internal events, such as our Company All Hands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the AV experience at Stripe is equitable and consistent across the globe by leveraging remote managed technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the design, procurement, installation, and sign off of new office builds and retrofits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop run books and document processes to ensure repeat success for operational support teams and fellow Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work autonomously and navigate ambiguity to deliver on high impact projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with other teams at Stripe in supporting the future workplace&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expectation of travel to our offices as needed as it pertains to project work and high tiered event support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in an enterprise environment scaling build and deployment processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience delivering, developing, and writing complex technical solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level knowledge of AV hardware &amp;amp; software infrastructures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working consistently and effectively to collaborate within a global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of streaming and event production workflows and the necessary protocols.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design and support high complexity production spaces as well as standardized conference room systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with managing multiple vendors globally to ensure multiple overlapping projects are delivered on time&lt;/li&gt;
